        "in_reply_to": "",
        "content_type": "text/html",
        "body": "<div>\n<a href=\"https://zammad.avicennaresearch.com/#user/profile/478\" data-mention-user-id=\"478\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer noopener\" title=\"https://zammad.avicennaresearch.com/#user/profile/478\">Sara Farnya</a> <a href=\"https://zammad.avicennaresearch.com/#user/profile/53\" data-mention-user-id=\"53\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer noopener\" title=\"https://zammad.avicennaresearch.com/#user/profile/53\">Mojtaba Javan</a> I checked their logs, application state and device state throughly. It looks like the app is being killed as soon as it goes to background. I think <a href=\"https://zammad.avicennaresearch.com/#user/profile/313\" data-mention-user-id=\"313\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer noopener\" title=\"https://zammad.avicennaresearch.com/#user/profile/313\">Alireza Javan</a> should check this too, just to make sure I'm not missing something</div><div>They didn't have power saving enabled, memory and storage were not low, everything seems to be okay on their side, so I suspect they didn't disable battery optimization for Avicenna App.</div><div>I will reassign to Alireza just for double checking since they're an important client. <a href=\"https://zammad.avicennaresearch.com/#user/profile/313\" data-mention-user-id=\"313\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer noopener\" title=\"https://zammad.avicennaresearch.com/#user/profile/313\">Alireza Javan</a> You shouldn't answer them directly.<br>\n</div>",
